{"id": "EUVD-2026-66491", "enisaUuid": "e5375691-8336-3327-a709-74f557223a73", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdgpu: reject oversized IBs with per-ring packet limits\n\nOn GFX rings, amdgpu_cs_p2_ib() passed user-supplied ib_bytes through\nto ib->length_dw without a limit, while ring_emit_ib() encodes length\ninto packet fields. Oversized values can corrupt adjacent control bits\nand destabilize command submission.\n\nAdd a per-ring IB packet size limit helper and reject command\nsubmissions exceeding the corresponding dword limit before IB\nallocation. Use the documented 20-bit limit for GFX/compute/SDMA/VPE,\nand apply the MM fallback limit for other ring types.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 7f48fa2cf62e3fa6c9c3870aa74988f773247e52)", "datePublished": "2026-08-26T14:37:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:46:30", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/67a5d905c17a5066b0f6f950da11da93d56d122b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e164ba1057175fb8a370d8e05cbff5c57eac0c8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1474f3970d1afd303e12ff14d06808eabb371576", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/07fe270ec07c138a70afe7a81e115a85c35c545c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fd37f9dd5b5ab70a46fa7bc76623c0528d602b27"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80576", "GHSA-mv2f-pcc7-qh27"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0aba4a54-82cf-39df-a027-552be1f64d48", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d38ceaf99ed015f2a0b9af3499791bd3a3daae21 <07fe270ec07c138a70afe7a81e115a85c35c545c"}, {"id": "57db0013-6cd0-3f9e-b5fb-47dfd3e21d3e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d38ceaf99ed015f2a0b9af3499791bd3a3daae21 <1474f3970d1afd303e12ff14d06808eabb371576"}, {"id": "71b40f61-3641-3d8f-986c-e5f63c5bc759", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.10"}, {"id": "8ca42018-66ff-3fed-a36f-8bf659f4b559", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "9c36aef7-82f5-38bc-af29-74c79beaeaf5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d38ceaf99ed015f2a0b9af3499791bd3a3daae21 <6e164ba1057175fb8a370d8e05cbff5c57eac0c8"}, {"id": "a7189ef4-4bc9-3581-96b3-94fe68abc5b9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "cf28eb97-c84d-3345-bd22-0b854ea9f3c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "d413c7a4-94ce-3783-bfac-4659505c8c68", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d38ceaf99ed015f2a0b9af3499791bd3a3daae21 <fd37f9dd5b5ab70a46fa7bc76623c0528d602b27"}, {"id": "e47eef3f-0459-3f17-b67b-b1de090fa22f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.46"}, {"id": "e5800c57-f278-3671-a561-2bea1de5bd82", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d38ceaf99ed015f2a0b9af3499791bd3a3daae21 <67a5d905c17a5066b0f6f950da11da93d56d122b"}, {"id": "ed4d5e23-1483-3e1a-bfc3-a26a865a61a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.2"}, {"id": "ff5340f1-9c62-3ada-a223-3622f4383181", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.105"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8025a2e3-37d4-3194-aafa-52d913993f86", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}